.\" Keep this page current: it describes the demo game demos/river.bas (an executable made with BUILD, installed by "make install").
.TH ENGINE1999-RIVER 6 "November 2026" "Engine 1999 @VERSION@" "Engine1999 Manual"
.SH NAME
engine1999-river \- Eternal River, a scroll-down boat game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B engine1999-river
.SH DESCRIPTION
Eternal River is a scroll-down boat game in the spirit of River Raid. You steer a boat down a river that meanders and never ends. Swimmers, divers and other boats are in the way, and people on the banks throw rocks at you. Now and then a bridge crosses the river, with people, a bicycle and cars on it, just for decoration: you pass under it (and score 100 points). The banks are lined with meadows, trees, villages and roads.
.PP
A hit is a matter of luck: you may be wrecked, or you may only be thrown into the water. Then swim to a bank (the swimming time is limited), walk along it (the river scrolls as you walk up), pick up the apples, carrots and ice cream cones you find, and look for a boat: one moored at a jetty, or one that was left drifting. The river gets narrower and busier with the distance (every 4000 pixels is a new level), and you get an extra life for every 5000 points.
.PP
The program is the demo \fIriver.bas\fR of Engine1999, made into an executable with
.B BUILD
(window kind: it needs the SDL2 library, nothing else); its BASIC libraries are inside it. It opens the Engine1999 window; the window can
be switched between the full screen and a window with F11 or ALT+RETURN.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.BR LEFT / RIGHT " or " A / D
steer the boat (swim, walk).
.TP
.BR UP " or " W
faster; walking: walk on (the river scrolls).
.TP
.BR DOWN " or " S
slower.
.TP
.B SPACE
walking: jump into the water.
.TP
.B P
pause.
.TP
.B Q
quit.
.PP
A game controller works, too: D-pad or left stick steers, A jumps, START pauses, BACK quits.
.SH FILES
The best score is kept in the file
.I river.hi
in the current directory (the game goes on without it if the file cannot be written).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine1999 (1),
.BR engine1999-basic (7)
